    },
    "body": "I think maybe we should invert the wording here: prefetch.i _should_ be authorized by PCC, but to allow easier implementation in complex microarchitectures it _may_ be authorized by ddc instead. The downside of using ddc is of course that it might not cover the code segment which then renders the instruction useless. For now ddc mostly covers the PCC range but if you use it for hybrid sandboxes I imagine it generally won't... \n\nNot sure what the best solution here is? No checks at all? Use a stale/predicted PCC? ",
